abstract: >-
  Data and code for a fixed-checkpoint audit of local decision geometry in a
  SpikeSCR classifier on Spiking Speech Commands. The repository holds the
  frozen checkpoint, the 100-source audit panel, the complete outcome map of
  725,070 adjacent-bin neighbors, activation-change metrics at seven boundaries,
  180,740 clean-activation replacement score vectors, the search-policy records,
  the outcomes of two count-readout replicas and the execution-control records,
  together with a package that regenerates every manuscript table from these
  files and compares 434 printed values with their regenerated counterparts.
  Project software is licensed under MIT; project-authored research outputs,
  documentation and model weights under CC BY 4.0, within the author's rights.
  Dataset attribution and third-party software terms remain in force; see
  LICENSE_NOTICE.md.
keywords:
  - spiking neural networks
  - speech recognition
  - Spiking Speech Commands
  - SpikeSCR
  - local decision geometry
  - activation replacement
  - execution controls
  - reproducible research
